<title>USA: Silicon's Cray gets 3 supercomputer orders.</title>
<headline>Silicon's Cray gets 3 supercomputer orders.</headline>
<dateline>EAGAN, Minn. 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cray Research, a subsidiary of Silicon Graphics Inc, said Thursday it received orders for three Cray Research Supercomputers from the Department of Defense Naval Oceanographic office.</p>
<p>These supercomputers, two Cray T3E-900 systems and one Cray T932 system, were purchased through system integrator Northrop Grumman's Corp's Data Systems &amp; Services Division and will perform a wide range of oceanographic modeling, prediction and data collection applications.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
